Rapid Connection is a [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] of [[Org/Prime Meridian/index|Prime Meridian]] that helps run the trains of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]]. It is one of three great Hearts Prime Meridian installed to coordinate [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]]'s transport about a century ago. [[People/Hogan Voss Darkmoor|Archmechanic Darkmoor]] keeps it. It likes trains, and it collects paintings, oil or acrylic on canvas.

Its fane lies under the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus|Sub Transit Nexus]], down a slow freight elevator: a circular stone path over thousands of gears of the same dull metal that runs in the Org's rods, each turning or reversing on its own rather than in the steady march of a watch. Rapid Connection has no mouth. It speaks by working its gears against one another into tones that copy human speech, or through mouthpieces, or through car radios on a dead frequency, 980.2 on the AM dial. The Party are the only people outside the Org ever let in to see it.

Its servants are wired like the rest of the Org's staff, with rods and piping of dull metal driven into their skin and their throats. They meet sellers in a partitioned loading bay at the nexus.

Its collection includes the [[People/Kellum Quinn|Kellum Quinn]] *Second Meaning*. The Heart stripped the outer paint away, and under the skyline of the Aurideon the painting hid the [[Pharos]], covered over.

Rapid Connection held keystone 14, the one nearest the [[Sin and Tonic]], and gave it to the Party in exchange for the painting and their promise to bring it any art they find. The stone is a cut blue gem like a plumb bob, kept in an ornate golden box; [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] reads it as a key to a sealed compartment of some kind, with something in it that only receives. The Heart has also waived all Prime Meridian fees for the Party's travel, roads as well as rails.
